# PART 15 — MILK INVENTORY AND RECONCILIATION

Implement a stock-movement ledger.

Movement types may include:
- Opening balance.
- Own production.
- Purchased milk accepted.
- Sale.
- Waste.
- Rejected or damaged stock.
- Eligible return.
- Authorized adjustment.
- Other outflow.

Every movement should include:
- Unique ID.
- Business date.
- Quantity.
- Unit.
- Movement type.
- Source record.
- Created by.
- Notes.
- Correction or reversal reference where relevant.

Use signed quantities consistently or store direction explicitly. Document the chosen convention.

Stock formula:

Available stock = opening stock + production + accepted purchases + eligible returns + approved inflows.

Closing stock = available stock - sales - waste - other outflows.

Display:
- Opening stock.
- Production.
- Purchased quantity.
- Available quantity.
- Sold quantity.
- Waste.
- Other outflows.
- Closing stock.
- Physical count.
- Difference between calculated and physical stock.

Prevent duplicate posting of the same source transaction.

Do not allow an ordinary UI edit to erase or duplicate a stock movement.

If stock becomes insufficient:
- Block the operation or require explicit authorized resolution.
- Show the shortage.
- Identify which operation caused it.
- Do not silently create negative stock.

Treat a return as saleable only when explicitly approved under the configured return policy.

Keep the prototype stock ledger separate from a future batch-traceability system. Do not claim full batch traceability unless lot tracking is actually implemented.

