# PART 26 — VALIDATION AND EDGE CASES

Explicitly implement and test the following behaviors:

1. Sold listings cannot appear as available.
2. Reservation cancellation requires an explicit status transition.
3. Concurrent edits must not silently overwrite newer values.
4. Missing optional animal information must not create fake values.
5. Price ranges must be valid and nonnegative.
6. Milk production must not be posted twice.
7. Collection quantities must distinguish received, accepted and rejected milk.
8. Corrections must not duplicate stock movements.
9. Daily subscription generation must be idempotent.
10. Paused subscriptions must not generate future deliveries.
11. Historical delivery records must not change after future subscription edits.
12. Actual delivery quantities must be recorded independently of scheduled quantities.
13. Stock shortages must be visible.
14. Negative stock must be prevented or explicitly resolved by authorized staff.
15. Duplicate stock movements must be prevented.
16. Customer payments must not be counted twice.
17. Supplier payments must not be confused with customer receipts.
18. Partial payments must preserve outstanding balances.
19. Historical rates must remain unchanged for existing transactions.
20. Payment reversals must preserve audit history.
21. Invalid routes must show a useful error page.
22. Restricted actions must be hidden or disabled appropriately in the prototype.
23. Public pages must not expose private operational information.
24. Failed form submissions must preserve useful user input where safe.
25. Empty states must provide a meaningful next action.
26. Missing or broken media must not break the layout.
27. All major workflows must work at mobile widths.
28. Date calculations must use the configured business timezone.
29. Dashboard totals must reconcile with source records.
30. Failed mock operations must provide visible error feedback.

